+# Task 4 review fix round 1 — timestamp metadata correction
+
+
+Read the full Task 4 review. Spec compliance failed on one P2 register timestamp defect; code quality passed and the actual isolated compatibility checkpoint remains supported. Verified the exact cited index row and manifest before preparing a change. E-T4-ARTIFACTS carried `2026-10-06T00:56:06.459382+00:00`, preceding the referenced manifest generation at `2026-10-06T00:57:41.427989+00:00`. The manifest bytes/hash and native output evidence are sound; the defect is carried-forward provenance timing.
+
+Fresh clock-tool observations bracket the local existing-manifest hash check at 01:04:49–01:05:11 UTC. `runtime/results/timestamp-correction-clock.json` records those actual new observation times. The patch proposes `2026-10-06T01:05:11+00:00` as the corrected observation timestamp, explicitly a fresh verification of the existing body rather than a recreated original capture, new execution or new manifest generation. Manifest SHA-256 remains `9b01b2e0256a869ae37b8a097e2f7ace9ef25a884157d2fe0afee0fdddbc569b`.
+
+Owned correction artifacts have only the `runtime/results/timestamp-correction-*` prefix. `timestamp-correction-old-index.csv` retains exact original index bytes, SHA-256 `89abcf061195f39d77b4c0c5bdc448633565c51196413d45418cef5f58a0dcf1`; `timestamp-correction-patch.json` retains the exact old/new row dictionaries, raw CSV row bytes/hashes, reason, clock/source provenance, strict old-index precondition and expected new-index SHA-256 `afc6cf2504f55f931a0f7b95c0cabf8871b3f42d8421b46a3d00b0cb1e691ea2`. It changes exactly one cell, accessed_or_received_at_utc, leaving every other row field and byte unchanged. Root owns the shared index apply and separately froze its exact old index version.
+
+Fresh command `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/runtime/results/timestamp-correction-check.py --pre` exits 0. Its complete argv/timestamps/stdout/stderr/exit code are retained in `timestamp-correction-pre.command.json`, `.stdout.json` and `.stderr.txt`. The read-only checker independently confirms unchanged manifest hash/generation, fresh observation after generation, exact old-index/row preservation and that the prospective exact-byte replacement changes only the named timestamp cell. No manifest, current indexed runtime artifact, retained report copy or proposal file was regenerated or mutated; no container rerun, Azure/SEC/network access occurred.
+
+Root must now apply the reviewed exact-byte patch, then run the same checker with --post and the existing check_index_reference_hashes.py, retaining their actual output/exit codes. This appendix currently reports prepared/precheck success only; post-apply and scoped re-review are pending before Task 5.
+
+### Fix round 1 applied and freshly checked
+
+Root froze the original index and applied the reviewed exact-byte timestamp replacement. Its retained timestamp-correction-root-apply receipt and current direct SHA-256 confirm expected new index `afc6cf2504f55f931a0f7b95c0cabf8871b3f42d8421b46a3d00b0cb1e691ea2`. Fresh direct inspection still confirms manifest SHA-256 `9b01b2e0256a869ae37b8a097e2f7ace9ef25a884157d2fe0afee0fdddbc569b`; the manifest body/generation and all other row values remain unchanged.
+
+Root ran `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/runtime/results/timestamp-correction-check.py --post`: exit 0, exact current index bytes equal the one-cell replacement, corrected timestamp `2026-10-06T01:05:11+00:00` is after manifest generation, and original row/index bytes and unchanged manifest hash verify. Full argv/timestamps/stdout/stderr/exit code are in timestamp-correction-post.command.json, .stdout.json and .stderr.txt.
+
+Root ran `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/investigation-tools/check_index_reference_hashes.py`: exit 0, all 180 local artifact references across 180 index rows verify. Full argv/timestamps/stdout/stderr/exit code are in timestamp-correction-index-reference.command.json, .stdout.json and .stderr.txt. This agent inspected those actual retained outputs and exit codes before reporting the correction complete.
+
+The fix changes provenance metadata only, with an explicit new observation rather than an earlier original capture. No indexed runtime report copy, artifact manifest, dependency/probe evidence or proposals were mutated; no manifest regeneration, native probe rerun, Azure/SEC/network access occurred. This fix appendix alone is separately retained as runtime/results/timestamp-correction-fix-report.md. Scoped re-review remains the root gate before Task 5; no spec-pass or Stage 1 readiness verdict is inferred from the metadata checks.
